The function is already minimal, so the only win is to steer the branch predictor and code layout: mark the two early-exit conditions as unlikely so the valid path stays straight-line and the loads for `numFields`/`numSubFields` are not speculated against a cold branch.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == NULL, 0) ||
        __builtin_expect(profileIndex >= profile->numFields, 0))
        return 0;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].numSubFields;
}
```